# Interpolated value types, 8 frames over 1s, linear ease (frame 8 is at t=7/8). Each cell is a quadrant of the 96x96 artboard.
# Top left: a 24x24 rect with an ink outline whose fill goes from red to blue through OKLab: red in frame 1, purple in the middle frames (not gray), mostly blue in frame 8.
# Top right: a green 64-sided poly, round like a circle, centered at x=72, y=24 that grows from r 4 in frame 1 to r 12.75 in frame 8 (a number key).
# Bottom left: a gold 28x12 rect centered at x=24, y=72 that rotates from 0 to 78.75 degrees: horizontal in frame 1, tilted 11.25 degrees further each frame (an angle key).
# Bottom right: a blue circle (r 6) that moves along the diagonal from (66,66) in frame 1 to (83.5,83.5) in frame 8 (a vector key), clear of the blend lens in the center.
# Center: a pale blue circle r 10 at x=56, y=48 is drawn first; a pale red circle r 10 at x=48, y=48 over it uses blend:key(normal multiply multiply),
# so the overlap lens is plain pale red in frames 1-4 and a darker purple in frames 5-8: a word steps at once and never fades. Undocumented, current behavior: a stepped value holds each key until the next, so the blend changes at frame 5 (t=.5s), the middle key.
@artboard 96x96
@target anim/key_types.gif fps:8 dur:1s

rect 24x24 at:24,24 fill:p.red.3 stroke:p.ink,1 name:tint
poly 64 r:4 at:72,24 fill:p.green stroke:p.ink,1 name:grow
rect 28x12 at:24,72 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,1 name:spin
circle 6 at:66,66 fill:p.blue stroke:p.ink,1 name:slide
circle 10 at:56,48 fill:p.blue.3
circle 10 at:48,48 fill:p.red.3 name:lens
anim types dur:1s
  .tint fill:key(p.red.3 p.blue.3 ease:linear)
  .grow r:key(4 14 ease:linear)
  .spin rot:abs(key(0 90 ease:linear))
  .slide at:abs(key(66,66 86,86 ease:linear))
  .lens blend:key(normal multiply multiply)
play types
